  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x341E" flags="0x0">
    <title>Fuel Targets</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0xB33A; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Control 2D table: its output is an offset-encoded byte with neutral 128; when flag 0x40 is set, it forms a saturated difference with the output of 0000ab4a as clamp_u8(this - map_0000ab4a + 128), otherwise it is passed through directly. Control 2D table: its output is an offset-encoded byte with neutral 128; when flag 0x40 is set, it forms a saturated difference with the output of 0000ab4a as clamp_u8(this - map_0000ab4a + 128), otherwise it is passed through directly. Result disposition: writes. Result target: ffff1c5d. Machine trace: 0000b33a[uint8 128..178] -&gt; 000bfe22/000261b8 -&gt; 00026770/00026944/00026c78/00026740 -&gt; 000bfe28 extu.b. ffff2466[0x40]=0 -&gt; 000bfe2e/000bfe30 -&gt; 000bfe6c -&gt; ffff1c5d. ffff2466[0x40]=1 -&gt; 000bfe4c(0000ab4a, uint8 128..148) -&gt; 000bfe50/000bfe52: this-other -&gt; 000bfe54/000bfe56: +128 -&gt; 000bfe58..000bfe68: clamp 0..255 -&gt; 000bfe6c -&gt; ffff1c5d. For the actual ranges, the difference path yields 108..178. 000bfe88 reads ffff1c5d through DAT_000c0284+DAT_000c01e6 and then explicitly treats 0x80 as the neutral state. The tuner-facing gasoline-AFR projection is candidate evidence from the HR A2L and the UpRev/EcuTek fuel-target descriptions rather than this code trace. Formula 1881.6/x maps raw 128 to 14.70 AFR, raw 168 to 11.20 AFR, and raw 178 to 10.57 AFR. Physical identity remains unverified on JK08A hardware.</description>
