  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xAA84" flags="0x0">
    <title>Calculated Load</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x1491A; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Sixteen-point uint16 normalization reference for the calculated-load byte. Lookup M by uint8[ffff11b3]&lt;&lt;8 enters q=floor((uint16[ffff1024]&lt;&lt;8)/M); an optional second normalization uses ffff329f, and the result is clamped to 255 and written to ffff413e for J1979 Mode 01 PID 0x04. The exact image closes both wrapper branches: 000263f4 calls the complete uint16 interpolation path in 00026a60/00026740 for coordinates below 0xf000 and returns cell 15 otherwise. FUN_0008083c calculates the load code, optionally applies floor((q&lt;&lt;7)/uint8[ffff329f]) when ROM8[0x870e] bit 4 is set, clamps to 255, and writes ffff413e. FUN_00035856 returns this byte for PID 0x04; standard conversion is 100*A/255. The operational 100% normalization role has code confidence. The BFS unit, x*0.000488 scale, and static RPM axis come from the HR A2L catalog and remain candidate. Static diagnostic context: CAL/LD VALUE [code, homologous_vq35hr, via map evidence: writes].</description>
